## Completion Summary (2026-05-13)

The original handoff's §3 schema (separate `image-gen` / `video-gen` buckets co-equal
with the six tier buckets) was **not implemented as drawn**. The implementation took a
cleaner path: the existing visual capability slots (`image_generates`, `image_edits`,
`video_generates`, etc.) are already provider-scoped, so adding OpenRouter as a
provider directly on those slots achieved the same end without inflating the bucket
namespace. The tier buckets remain at seven (`local-premium`, `local-mid`,
`local-fast`, `premium`, `mid`, `fast`, `free`) with friendly display labels (Large /
Medium / Small / Premium / Mid / Fast / Free) — not eight.

### What actually shipped

The session executed a roadmap that the user iterated mid-session — substantially
larger than the §3 sketch:

1. **Tier label fix.** UI was hardcoded to `local-large` / `local-small` (which had
   no data); pipeline references to `local-premium` / `local-mid` were invisible.
   Replaced with a `TIER_LABELS` display map; internal plumbing unchanged.

2. **Settings tab restructure.** Models tab split into three tabs: **Models**
   (pipelines only, 2-column), **Buckets** (the bucket panel, standalone), **Visual**
   (image/video capabilities in a 3-column grid). ConfigPanel grew a `view:` config
   option that switches between the four layouts (`pipelines` / `buckets` / `visual` /
   legacy `all`).

3. **Pipeline presets.** Named snapshots of `pipelines` + `buckets` + `diversity` at
   `~/ora/config/pipeline-presets.json`. Dropdown + Save / Save As… / Delete buttons
   at the top of the Models tab. Activate-preset endpoint writes preset values to
   `routing-config.json` and reloads the boot router. Visual prefs intentionally NOT
   captured per preset (treated as permanent global).

4. **OpenRouter foundation.** `~/ora/scripts/refresh-openrouter.py` fetches the
   catalog across all 8 modalities via the public `output_modalities` query param
   (text 363 · image 20 · video 13 · speech 8 · transcription 6 · audio 5 · embedding
   25 · rerank 3). Writes a normalized 431-model catalog to
   `~/ora/config/openrouter-catalog.json` with vendor + modality indices and
   per-million-token pricing. Server endpoints: `GET /config/openrouter/catalog`,
   `POST /config/openrouter/refresh`. Auto-refreshes on server startup if catalog is
   older than 7 days. `_call_openrouter()` added to
   `~/ora/orchestrator/tools/api_evaluate.py`.

5. **Slot-fill picker (Buckets tab).** Replaced the ordered-list-per-tier UI with a
   2-slot mechanic — Primary + (Adversarial / Fallback depending on diversity
   toggle). Bucket cards in a 2×4 grid: Local row on top (Large / Medium / Small +
   placeholder), Commercial row below (Premium / Mid / Fast / Free). Picker source
   lists below each row — **Available — Local / Subscription / Direct API /
   OpenRouter**. OpenRouter text-models picker is a 4-column vendor accordion (59
   vendors), click-to-expand. Click a slot to arm it, click a model to fill it.

5b. **Direct-API model refreshers.** `~/ora/scripts/refresh-direct-apis.py` discovers
    new models via Anthropic, OpenAI, and Google `/v1/models` endpoints. Reconciles
    against existing routing-config endpoints by `model_id` AND by `_base_alias` (so
    user's dated pins like `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` stay valid when only the stable
    alias is published upstream). Adds new models; marks vanished ones
    `status: deprecated` (doesn't delete — slot references stay readable). Auto-runs
    on server startup if older than 7 days. Manual "Refresh from vendors" button on
    the Direct API picker section. Filters out non-text variants (TTS, audio,
    realtime, image, embedding) and dated snapshots from the picker view.

6. **Transcription tab.** Whisper tab renamed and expanded. Provider dropdown switches
   among: Local Whisper / OpenRouter transcription / OpenRouter audio understanding.
   When OpenRouter STT is selected: model picker (6 transcription models). When audio
   understanding: model picker (5 native-audio-input models) + customizable Default
   Question field ("Transcribe this audio verbatim" by default; user can change to
   "Summarize the key points" etc.). Backend: `transcription.py::_run` branches on
   provider — local Whisper path unchanged, OpenRouter paths use OpenAI SDK with
   `base_url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`. Verified end-to-end against a 30-second
