### Chat empty-response root cause + fix (resolved)

`server.py:_pipeline_stream` was running the analytical pipeline against the placeholder modes `simple` and `standard` for three different paths (Stage-1 bypass, Stage-2 catch-all, Stage-2 pending-clarification on the plain-HTTP endpoint). Both placeholder mode files were Phase-9-archived; `load_mode()` returns `""`; pipeline finishes with no response event; collector sees `final_response=None, failure_summary=None` → marks errored with "pipeline produced no response."

Fix: 8-line guard at the top of `_pipeline_stream` falls all three paths through to `_direct_stream` (which calls the model with `boot.md` as system prompt and yields a real `response` event). The analytical pipeline still runs for prompts that successfully dispatch to a real mode (terrain-mapping, root-cause-analysis, etc.). Verified end-to-end with both "hi" (clean conversational reply) and a SQL/NoSQL tradeoff question (real pipeline, ~10s).

